WEBVTT

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:02.204
Here's one of the organisms
that we caught in our net.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.487
This is a jellyfish.

00:01:03.881 --> 00:01:05.193
But look closely,

00:01:05.217 --> 00:01:08.208
and living inside of this animal
is another organism

00:01:08.232 --> 00:01:10.937
that is very likely
entirely new to science.

00:01:10.961 --> 00:01:12.639
A complete new species.

00:01:13.117 --> 00:01:15.820
Or how about this other transparent beauty

00:01:15.844 --> 00:01:17.384
with a beating heart,

00:01:17.408 --> 00:01:20.836
asexually growing on top of its head,

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:24.046
progeny that will move on
to reproduce sexually.

00:01:24.547 --> 00:01:26.034
Let me say that again:

00:01:26.058 --> 00:01:29.744
this animal is growing asexually
on top of its head,

00:01:29.768 --> 00:01:34.255
progeny that is going to reproduce
sexually in the next generation.